# --- Keep these OFF the public website (GitHub Pages serves everything else) ---

# Admin panel: contains the admin password + Cloudinary secret. Run it locally only.
# Wildcard is deliberate — the old exact-name rule missed admin_panel_edited.html
# and it stayed tracked for 330 commits. Any admin_panel* variant is now ignored.
admin_panel*.html

# Contributor review console (6 Aug 2026). Displays applicants' government ID
# photos, phone numbers and email addresses. Admin-only, run locally — the
# same reasoning as admin_panel*.html above, but the data is more sensitive:
# a leaked admin page is our problem, a leaked ID is the applicant's problem.
contributor_review.html

# Contributor payout console (9 Aug 2026). Shows every contributor's name,
# email and earnings, and records payouts. Same reasoning as above — admin
# only, run locally. A leaked admin page is our problem; a leaked page listing
# what other people are owed is theirs.
contributor_payouts.html

# BOTH of the above now live OUTSIDE this repository, in WebMarketplace/admin-local/
# (moved 9 Aug 2026). These two rules are kept anyway: if either file is ever
# copied back into the website folder by accident, git will still refuse to
# publish it. A belt-and-braces rule costs nothing; a leaked payout list does.

# Backend source (Google Apps Script). Lives in the Apps Script editor, not the site.
*.gs

# Metadata codec — PRIVATE. Never expose field/value codes to public.
# This file is the secret key to the LazyDog metadata encoding system.
meta_codec.py
firebase/functions/meta_codec.py

# Compiled Python — bytecode of the private files leaks the same secrets!
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# FULL editor source (parser+writer+all) — THE BRAIN. Never ever public.
editor_brain.html

# User data export — private
firebase/users.json

# Backend function source — deploys via `firebase deploy`, git never needs it.
# The whole folder, not a list of filenames: resume_fill.py was added on
# 12 Aug 2026 and, because only main.py was named here, it was committed and
# then served at lazydogtemplates.com/firebase/functions/resume_fill.py for
# anyone to read. No key leaked (those come from .env), but the prompts and the
# logic did. A directory rule cannot be forgotten the next time a file is added.
firebase/functions/
!firebase/functions/requirements.txt

# Lazydog Engine (Cloud Run) source — PRIVATE. Deploys via gcloud from this
# folder; git never needs it. server.py carries an Apps Script token and the
# whole metadata pipeline logic. (20 Aug 2026 — meta_codec.py was already
# ignored by name, but server.py and the rest of the folder were not.)
editor-v2/engine/

# Dissolve service (Cloud Run) source — PRIVATE, same rule as the engine.
# Deploys via gcloud; git never needs it. Caught 20 Aug 2026 one commit before
# it went public. Test decks/pdfs are just repo bloat — also kept out.
editor-v2/dissolve/
editor-v2/test_files/

# Common local-only / sensitive files
*.bak
*.tmp
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Buyer autofill system — PRIVATE brain/heart, never expose on the public site ---
fit_engine.js
buyer_flow_test.html
editor_opus.html
content_fitter.py

# AI cascade — private, deploy to Firebase but never GitHub
ai_fill.py
firebase/functions/ai_fill.py

# Word source of va_dictionary.js — reference only, keep off public site
va_dictionary.docx
lazydog-editor.html
